 s.\n\nOrganisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\
 , funded by Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antw
 erp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, R
 eykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early De
 c 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states
 \, Horizon Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, S
 outh Africa\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: 
 EUR 1\,000 flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange 
 Programme: EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, works
 hops or 2-day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start 
 of December 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/
 opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
